<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Recoverability Test</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix C Recoverability Test ‣ Off-Trajectory Reasoning: Can LLMs Collaborate on Reasoning Trajectory?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> reports a breakdown of model recoverability performance on shared subset across different positions (<math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>%</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\%</annotation></semantics></math>) of the original trajectories. Table <a href="#A3.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Appendix C Recoverability Test ‣ Off-Trajectory Reasoning: Can LLMs Collaborate on Reasoning Trajectory?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> reports the results of ablation study explained in §<a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Results ‣ 3 Off-the-shelf Evaluation &amp; Results ‣ Off-Trajectory Reasoning: Can LLMs Collaborate on Reasoning Trajectory?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, where the first paragraph of model reasoning is preserved. The subscripts in Table <a href="#A3.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Appendix C Recoverability Test ‣ Off-Trajectory Reasoning: Can LLMs Collaborate on Reasoning Trajectory?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> equals the difference between the major numbers in Table minus the corresponding numbers in Table <a href="#A3.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix C Recoverability Test ‣ Off-Trajectory Reasoning: Can LLMs Collaborate on Reasoning Trajectory?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> to show the changes in recoverability induced by the small tweak in trajectory.</p>
</div>
